 expected position.\n\n<img width=\"1854\" height=\"944\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/674c5554-eb16-4385-a450-89c92cc22e94\" />\n\nThis seems to be a symptom of Window.position not being set properly during window creation, my best guess being somewhere in `platform/linuxbsd/x11/display_server_x11.cpp`, causing windows to be placed incorrectly. `rect_changed_callback` seems to not be called at all after being set.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nRun the scene `test.tscn`.\nPress the 'Show popup' button.\nPress the 'OptionButtoon' and see if the selection pops up in the correct place or on the top left of your screen.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26219140/test.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117796/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117796/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}